| 731 | Small surplus of product 0 and only modest shortages | best, 0 |\n| 1 | daily | 855 | 731 | Order fees +559, holding −373 | about −190 |\n| 5 | 3 days | 854 | 696 | Order fees −215, holding +370, a little short on product 1 | about −250 |\n| 7 | 2 days | 743 | 731 | About 34 short on product 0 on average, plus extra shortages from day-to-day swings | about −460 |\n| 4 | 4 days | 854 | 658 | Very heavy holding of product 1; leftovers can't carry over | about −650 |\n| 3 | 2 days | 965 | 622 | About 190 extra product 0 spoils; about 143 short on product 1 | about −1100 |\n| 0 | 2 days | 1078 | 840 | About 300 extra product 0 spoils (about 1200), plus holding a large stock and excess product 1 | about −1200 |\n| 2 | 3 days | 966 | 622 | Same over/under pattern as candidate 3, plus 3-day holding costs | about −1200 |\n\n**Robustness to random demand**\n- Candidate 6 orders slightly above expected demand. Its stock builds slowly and absorbs swings, so it holds up best.\n- Candidate 7 orders just below expected demand. Its stock stays near zero, so random spikes turn directly into penalties.\n- The weakest call is candidate 7 against candidate 4, because the estimated gap between them is only about 190. So both get probabilities close to 0.5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5052, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5052}, "output_tokens": 9, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T07:51:08.766Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWAMEwxVAubeL91FwKEG"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_star